---
title: 'épisode 12 : bilan'
tags:
  - fr
  - language
  - learning
---

Q: In the printemps bilan, what does a `question fermée` let the other person answer?
A: {{`Oui`}} or {{`non`}}, a yes/no answer.
N: [[fr/episode-12#exercice-3--les-questions-fermées|Questions fermées]], manuel p. 88.

---

C: Valérie [fait|faire, présent] du café.
N: Manuel p. 88, exercice 2. [[fr/episode-12]]

---

C: Jérémie [écoute|écouter, présent] de la musique.
N: The verb agrees with the singular subject Jérémie. Manuel p. 88.

---

C: Valérie et Jérémie [mangent|manger, présent] ensemble.
N: Two people give a plural subject, equivalent to `ils`. Manuel p. 88.

---

C: Valérie [va|aller, présent] au travail.
N: Manuel p. 88. `Aller` is irregular. [[fr/episode-12]]

---

C: Jérémie [va|aller, présent] à la garderie.
N: Manuel p. 88. `La garderie` means daycare.

---

C: Après leur journée, Valérie et Jérémie [rentrent|rentrer, présent] à la maison.
N: Manuel p. 88. `Rentrer` means to return or come home here.

---

C: Valérie et Jérémie [jouent|jouer, présent] ensemble.
N: Manuel p. 88. `Ensemble` means together.

---

C: Pendant que Valérie prépare le souper, Jérémie [dessine|dessiner, présent].
N: Manuel p. 88. `Le souper` is the evening meal in Québec.

---

C: Dans la première image de la p. 88, l'homme [lit|lire, présent].
N: `Il lit.` The infinitive is `lire`. [[fr/episode-12]]

---

Q: Make `Tu joues du piano.` a yes/no question with `est-ce que`.
A: {{`Est-ce que tu joues du piano ?`}}
N: Manuel p. 88, exercice 3. Keep subject–verb order after `est-ce que`.

---

Q: Make `Tu joues du piano.` a yes/no question using inversion.
A: {{`Joues-tu du piano ?`}}
N: Manuel p. 88. The conjugated verb and subject pronoun are joined by a hyphen.

---

Q: Make `Tu joues du piano.` a spoken Québec yes/no question with interrogative `-tu`.
A: {{`Tu joues-tu du piano ?`}}
N: The first `tu` is the subject; the second is an interrogative particle. Manuel p. 88.

---

Q: Make `Tu travailles toute la journée.` a yes/no question using inversion.
A: {{`Travailles-tu toute la journée ?`}}
N: Manuel p. 88. The verb stays in its `tu` form, including the written `-s`.

---

Q: Make `Tu relaxes.` a yes/no question with `est-ce que`.
A: {{`Est-ce que tu relaxes ?`}}
N: Manuel p. 88. `Relaxer` means to relax; it follows the regular `-er` pattern.

---

Q: Make `Tu lis un roman.` a yes/no question using inversion.
A: {{`Lis-tu un roman ?`}}
N: Manuel p. 88. `Lire` gives `tu lis` at the present.

---

Q: In `Elle lit-tu un roman ?`, does the interrogative `-tu` mean that the subject is “you”?
A: No. The subject is `elle`; `-tu` marks a spoken Québec yes/no question.
N: The particle stays `-tu` with different subjects. [[fr/episode-12#exercice-3--les-questions-fermées|Questions fermées]]

---

Q: Make `Il joue de la guitare.` a yes/no question using inversion.
A: {{`Joue-t-il de la guitare ?`}}
N: The linking `-t-` appears between `joue` and `il`. It differs from Québec interrogative `-tu`.

---

C: Au présent, je [vais] à la boulangerie, tu [vas] chez le dentiste et on [va] au café.
N: Manuel p. 89. Three singular forms of `aller`, used with three destinations.

---

C: Au présent, nous [allons] au café, vous [allez] au cinéma et elles [vont] à la piscine.
N: Review of `aller` for the destination exercise, manuel p. 89.

---

C: Tu vas [chez|destination: a person] le dentiste.
N: Manuel p. 89. `Chez` is used for the dentist's practice through the person.

---

C: On va [au|à + le] café avec nos amis.
N: Manuel p. 89. `À + le = au`.

---

C: Elles vont [à la|destination: la piscine] piscine.
N: Manuel p. 89. Feminine `la` stays separate after `à`.

---

C: Dans la piste 18, tu vas [à|transport preposition] pied et je vais [à|transport preposition] vélo.
N: `À pied`, on foot; `à vélo`, by bike. Manuel p. 89, transcription p. 137.

---

C: Dans la piste 18, on va au travail [en|transport preposition] métro et ils vont chez toi [en|transport preposition] autobus.
N: Manuel p. 89, transcription p. 137. These vehicles take `en` in this exercise.

---

Q: CD2 piste 18, statement 1: how do the people get to work?
A: {{`En métro.`}} The printed transcript says {{`On va au travail en métro.`}}
N: Manuel p. 89; transcription p. 137. [[fr/episode-12#piste-18--les-moyens-de-transport|Piste 18]]

---

Q: CD2 piste 18, statement 2: how does the person get to school?
A: {{`À pied.`}}
N: `Tu vas à l'école à pied.` Manuel p. 89; transcription p. 137.

---

Q: CD2 piste 18, statement 3: which transport is mentioned in the question about the airport?
A: {{`En taxi.`}}
N: `Allez-vous à l'aéroport en taxi ?` This is a question. Manuel p. 89; transcription p. 137.

---

Q: CD2 piste 18, statement 4: how do they get to the listener's place?
A: {{`En autobus.`}}
N: `Ils vont chez toi en autobus.` Manuel p. 89; transcription p. 137.

---

Q: CD2 piste 18, statement 5: how does the speaker get to the grocery store?
A: {{`À vélo.`}}
N: `Je vais à l'épicerie à vélo.` Manuel p. 89; transcription p. 137.

---

Q: Which means of transport appears in the piste 18 answer grid without being used in the five utterances?
A: {{`En train.`}}
N: The train appears in the next exercise, piste 19. Manuel p. 89.

---

Q: CD2 piste 19: at what time does the speaker take the train?
A: `À 7 h 30.`
N: `Je prends le train à 7 h 30.` Transcription p. 137.

---

Q: CD2 piste 19: approximately when does the speaker arrive at work?
A: `Vers 7 h 50.`
N: `J'arrive au travail vers 7 h 50.` Transcription p. 137.

---

Q: CD2 piste 19: at what time does the speaker have lunch?
A: {{`À midi.`}}
N: `Je dine à midi.` Transcription p. 137. `Diner` is the midday meal in Québec.

---

Q: CD2 piste 19: at what time does the speaker finish work?
A: `À 16 h.`
N: `Je finis mon travail à 16 h.` Transcription p. 137.

---

Q: CD2 piste 19: approximately when does the speaker cook?
A: `Vers 18 h.`
N: `Je fais la cuisine vers 18 h.` Transcription p. 137.

---

Q: CD2 piste 19: at what time does the speaker watch television?
A: `À 20 h.`
N: `Je regarde la télé à 20 h.` Transcription p. 137.

---

Q: In the bilan's time expressions, what distinction does `à 7 h 50` / `vers 7 h 50` express?
A: `À` gives a stated exact time; `vers` gives an approximate time, around 7:50.
N: Manuel p. 89. [[fr/episode-12#piste-19--les-heures|Piste 19]]

---

C: Pour dire « I take the train », on écrit `Je [prends] le train.`
N: Piste 19. `Prendre` gives `je prends`, `il prend`, `nous prenons`.

---

C: Pour dire « I finish my work », on écrit `Je [finis] mon travail.`
N: Piste 19. `Finir` gives `je finis`, `il finit`, `nous finissons`.

---

Q: In Stéphane's schedule, what do the blue activities represent?
A: {{`Les activités habituelles`}}, repeated or usual activities.
N: Manuel p. 89. Use forms such as `Le mardi, il travaille.`

---

Q: In Stéphane's schedule, what do the orange activities represent?
A: {{`Les activités ponctuelles`}}, activities on a particular occasion.
N: Manuel p. 89. Use forms such as `Vendredi soir, il va chez Julien.`

---

Q: For a recurring Tuesday routine, add the missing word: `… mardi, Stéphane travaille.`
A: {{`Le mardi, Stéphane travaille.`}}
N: Manuel p. 89. The definite article marks the recurring day in this exercise.

---

Q: Describe Stéphane's one-off Friday evening visit to Julien, using a day expression.
A: {{`Vendredi soir, il va au party chez Julien.`}}
N: Manuel p. 89. The bare day expresses the particular occasion here.

---

Q: At which recurring time does Stéphane go to the gym on Saturday?
A: `Le samedi à 10 h.`
N: Manuel p. 89. `Le samedi à 10 h, il va au gym.`

---

Q: Which meal does Stéphane have with his colleagues on Wednesday, according to the schedule?
A: {{`Le diner`}}, at midday: {{`Mercredi midi, il dine avec ses collègues.`}}
N: The corrigé's `Mercredi soir` conflicts with the midday placement of the activity. [[fr/episode-12#lhoraire-de-stéphane|Horaire de Stéphane]]

---

Q: In Québec, put `le déjeuner`, `le diner`, and `le souper` in day order.
A: {{`Le déjeuner`}} = breakfast; {{`le diner`}} = lunch; {{`le souper`}} = dinner/the evening meal.
N: These meal names determine how to read Stéphane's schedule. [[fr/episode-12]]

---

Q: Translate the map-reading instruction `Situez les endroits sur le plan.`
A: Locate the places on the map.
N: Manuel p. 90. `Un plan` means a map or layout here.

---

Q: On the p. 90 map, which place is the large brown building beside the playground?
A: `L'école` (label a).
N: [[fr/episode-12#le-plan-et-ses-six-repères|Le plan]], manuel p. 90.

---

Q: On the p. 90 map, which place is between the flower shop and the cinema?
A: {{`La banque`}} (label d).
N: The flower shop is `le fleuriste`; the cinema is `le cinéma`.

---

Q: On the p. 90 map, which place has the red roof and envelope symbol?
A: {{`Le bureau de poste`}} (label e).
N: Manuel p. 90. The location is on the boulevard des Riverains, beside the bank.

---

Q: On the p. 90 map, which place has the sombrero-shaped roof beside rue Légendre?
A: {{`Le restaurant mexicain`}} (label c).
N: Manuel p. 90. Use the visual landmark to locate it.

---

Q: On the p. 90 map, which place contains the swings beside the school?
A: {{`Le parc`}} (label f).
N: Manuel p. 90.

---

Q: On the p. 90 map, which place contains the outdoor pool beside rue Légendre?
A: {{`La piscine`}} (label b).
N: Manuel p. 90.

---

Q: CD2 piste 20: where do the directions starting at the cinema lead?
A: {{`Au fleuriste`}}, at the corner of rue Saint-Étienne and avenue Gignac.
N: Manuel p. 90; printed transcription p. 137.

---

Q: CD2 piste 20: in which direction do you turn when leaving the cinema?
A: {{`À votre gauche`}}, onto rue Saint-Étienne.
N: Printed transcription p. 137. [[fr/episode-12#piste-20--du-cinéma-au-fleuriste|Piste 20]]

---

Q: CD2 piste 20: which street do you cross before reaching avenue Gignac?
A: {{`La rue de l'Épée.`}}
N: Printed transcription p. 137.

---

C: Dans les indications, `Continuez [tout droit|straight ahead].`
N: Piste 20. `Tout droit` is a direction; `à droite` means to the right.

---

C: Le fleuriste est [au coin de|at the corner of] la rue Saint-Étienne et de l'avenue Gignac.
N: Piste 20, manuel p. 90.

---

Q: Turn `vous prenez` into a polite direction without a subject pronoun.
A: `Prenez.` For example: {{`Prenez la rue Saint-Étienne.`}}
N: The `vous` imperative keeps the verb form and removes the subject. [[fr/episode-12#demander-et-donner-un-trajet|Trajets]]

---

Q: Turn `vous traversez` into a polite direction without a subject pronoun.
A: `Traversez.` For example: {{`Traversez le pont Delisle.`}}
N: Review from [[fr/episode-10]], applied to the p. 90 map.

---

Q: Ask politely where the post office is, using `Pouvez-vous me dire…`.
A: {{`Pouvez-vous me dire où est le bureau de poste, s'il vous plait ?`}}
N: Model role-play for p. 90. After `où`, keep `est le bureau de poste` as the embedded location question.

---

Q: In the p. 90 service notice, does the change apply to every bus line?
A: `Non. Il concerne la ligne 4.`
N: The statement about `tous les autobus` is false. [[fr/episode-12#lavis-de-modification-de-service|Avis]]

---

Q: In the p. 90 service notice, does line 4 serve the avenue Théorêt stop during the works?
A: {{`Non. Il n'y a pas de service à cet arrêt.`}}
N: The statement `L'autobus n'arrête pas sur l'avenue Théorêt` is true.

---

Q: In the p. 90 service notice, is 8 h 20 a listed departure on rue Lemay?
A: `Non. L'heure affichée est 8 h.`
N: The statement about 20 June at 8 h 20 is false. Other listed times do not include 8 h 20.

---

Q: What is wrong with the notice's printed date range `du 1er au 31 juin`?
A: June has 30 days; `31 juin` is an impossible date.
N: Source typo, manuel p. 90. It does not change the exercise's false/true/false answers.

---

C: Un [arrêt|bus stop] d'autobus est un endroit où l'autobus s'arrête.
N: Service notice, manuel p. 90. The stop on avenue Théorêt has no service.

---

C: `En raison de travaux routiers` signifie [because of roadworks|English meaning].
N: Manuel p. 90. `En raison de` introduces the cause.

---

Q: In the p. 91 course pictures, which image shows the Spanish course?
A: {{`L'image b.`}}
N: Full mapping: dance a, Spanish b, cooking c, violin d. [[fr/episode-12#les-quatre-images-de-cours|Cours]]

---

C: Dans l'image d, c'est un cours de [violon|instrument], un instrument à cordes joué avec un archet.
N: Manuel p. 91. The bow is `un archet`.

---

Q: According to the p. 91 yoga advertisement, when is registration open?
A: `Du 1er au 15 juin.`
N: This registration window differs from the summer session, 16 June to 31 August.

---

Q: According to the p. 91 yoga advertisement, when does the summer session run?
A: `Du 16 juin au 31 aout.`
N: [[fr/episode-12#lannonce-corps-et-âme|Corps et âme]], manuel p. 91.

---

Q: According to the p. 91 yoga advertisement, how can you register?
A: {{`Sur place ou par téléphone.`}}
N: Internet registration is not offered in the advertisement.

---

Q: According to the p. 91 yoga advertisement, which payment methods are accepted?
A: {{`Comptant ou par chèque seulement.`}}
N: The claim about accepting cash or debit is false because debit is absent from the accepted methods.

---

Q: According to the p. 91 colour-coded yoga timetable, is there `yoga + bébé` on Saturday?
A: `Non.`
N: Green marks yoga + bébé; Saturday has purple and yellow cells only.

---

Q: According to the p. 91 yoga advertisement, what does one trial class cost a new client?
A: `10 $.`
N: `Un cours d'essai`, one trial class. The 17 \$ offer covers three discovery classes.

---

Q: According to the p. 91 yoga advertisement, what does the 17 \$ discovery offer include?
A: {{`Trois cours`}}, valid for one month, for new clients only.
N: It differs from the single 10 \$ trial class.

---

Q: In the yoga advertisement, what does `cours illimités` mean?
A: Unlimited classes.
N: The monthly subscription costs 125 \$ for one month or 330 \$ for three months. Manuel p. 91.

---

Q: In the yoga advertisement, what does `Les tarifs incluent les taxes` mean?
A: The prices include taxes.
N: Manuel p. 91. The stated price already includes the tax amount.

---

C: Pour la grossesse, on choisit le yoga [prénatal|course name].
N: The advertisement describes postures that relieve pregnancy discomfort. Manuel p. 91.

---

C: Le yoga + bébé s'adresse à la femme après [l'accouchement|childbirth].
N: Reading vocabulary from the advertisement, manuel p. 91.

---

Q: In `Trouvez qui…`, which answer words are allowed during the game?
A: Only `oui` or {{`non`}}.
N: Manuel p. 92–93. The teams discover missing activities through closed questions.

---

Q: In `Trouvez qui…`, what happens to the asking team's turn after a “non”?
A: It loses its turn; the other team asks a question.
N: After a “oui”, the same team asks another question. Manuel p. 93.

---

Q: Ask whether Max dances salsa on Tuesday evenings, using `est-ce que`.
A: {{`Est-ce que Max danse la salsa le mardi soir ?`}}
N: Fiche A's completed profile says yes. The recurring day takes `le`.

---

Q: Ask whether Jacques knits on weekends, using a rising-intonation question.
A: {{`Jacques tricote la fin de semaine ?`}}
N: Fiche A's completed profile says yes. `La fin de semaine` means the weekend in Québec.

---

Q: Ask whether Maude phones on Sunday afternoons, using `est-ce que`.
A: {{`Est-ce que Maude parle au téléphone le dimanche après-midi ?`}}
N: Fiche A's completed profile says yes. `Parler au téléphone` means to talk on the phone.

---

Q: Ask whether Jacques cooks every day, using `est-ce que`.
A: {{`Est-ce que Jacques fait la cuisine tous les jours ?`}}
N: Fiche B's completed profile says yes. `Tous les jours` means every day.

---

Q: Ask whether Woope-Laï speaks eight languages, using a spoken Québec `-tu` question.
A: {{`Woope-Laï parle-tu huit langues ?`}}
N: The particle is still `-tu` even with the named third-person subject. The completed profile says yes.

---

C: Dans le jeu, Max [va|aller, présent] au travail à vélo.
N: Completed fiche B. [[fr/episode-12#les-profils-complets|Profils complets]]

---

C: Dans le jeu, Rose [envoie|envoyer, présent] des courriels à sa sœur.
N: Completed fiche B. `Envoyer` changes `y` to `i` in `elle envoie`.

---

C: Dans le jeu, Maude [joue|jouer, présent] de la guitare.
N: Completed fiche B. `Jouer de` introduces an instrument.

---

C: Dans le jeu, Jacques joue [au|à + le] badminton.
N: Completed fiche B. `Jouer à` introduces this sport.

---

C: Dans le jeu, Jacques va [chez|destination: a person] sa fille le samedi matin.
N: `Chez sa fille` means to his daughter's place.

---

C: Dans le jeu, Woope-Laï [fait|faire, présent] une sieste l'après-midi.
N: `Faire une sieste` means to take a nap.

---

C: `Max lave [la vaisselle|the dishes] après le souper.`
N: Completed fiche A. `Laver la vaisselle` means to wash the dishes.

---

C: `Rose et Max passent [l'aspirateur|the vacuum cleaner] le matin.`
N: `Passer l'aspirateur` means to vacuum. Completed profiles in the p. 92–93 game.

---

C: `Woope-Laï fait [le ménage|the housework] le soir.`
N: `Faire le ménage` means to do the cleaning or housework. Completed fiche B.

---

Q: Translate `Rose fait une sieste l'avant-midi.` using the Québec time expression.
A: Rose takes a nap in the morning, before noon.
N: `L'avant-midi` is the period before noon; `l'après-midi` is after noon.

---

C: `Un [courriel|email]` est un message électronique.
N: Québec vocabulary in Rose's profile. `Elle envoie des courriels à sa sœur.`

---

Q: In the game, what distinguishes `Maude écoute de la musique` from `Maude joue de la guitare`?
A: `Écouter` means to listen; `jouer de` means to play an instrument.
N: Her complete profile says she listens to francophone music and plays the guitar.

---

Q: Describe Valérie and Jérémie together with the subject pronoun that replaces both names.
A: `Ils` : for example, {{`Ils mangent`}}, {{`ils rentrent à la maison`}}, {{`ils jouent ensemble`}}.
N: Manuel p. 88. The pair includes Jérémie, so the textbook uses `ils`.

---

Q: What does the bilan's instruction `Attribuez-vous une note` ask you to do?
A: Give yourself a score, with the help of a classmate or teacher where indicated.
N: The speaking tasks have model answers and are not marked by a single fixed sentence.
